<%- include('../partials/layout-start') %>
<%- include('../partials/page-header', {
  icon: 'bi-file-earmark-person',
  heading: 'Build your SAP CV',
  sub: 'From the profile you already filled in. No wizard, and nothing written for you.'
}) %>
<section class="glass-section pb-5">
<div class="container">
  <div class="row justify-content-center"><div class="col-lg-9">

    <div class="glass-card mb-4"><div class="card-body">
      <h2 class="h5 mb-3">There is no form to fill in twice</h2>
      <p>
        Your profile here already holds what a CV needs: the headline, the years, the full
        lifecycles, the skills, the certifications, the employment — and the delivery
        history, engagement by engagement, with the modules each one actually touched.
      </p>
      <p class="mb-0">
        So the CV is a rendering of that, produced when you click and never stored. It is
        always what your profile says at that moment, which means there is no second copy
        quietly going stale behind the one companies are searching.
      </p>
    </div></div>

    <div class="row g-3 mb-4">
      <div class="col-md-4">
        <div class="glass-card h-100"><div class="card-body">
          <span class="icon-tile icon-tile-sm icon-blue mb-2"><i class="bi bi-diagram-3"></i></span>
          <h3 class="h6 mb-1">It knows what a module is</h3>
          <p class="small text-muted-2 mb-0">
            A general CV builder cannot ask which modules an engagement touched, or which
            SAP Activate phase it ran in, because it has no idea those exist. This one puts
            them on the page.
          </p>
        </div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="col-md-4">
        <div class="glass-card h-100"><div class="card-body">
          <span class="icon-tile icon-tile-sm icon-success mb-2"><i class="bi bi-ui-checks"></i></span>
          <h3 class="h6 mb-1">Readable by the software that screens it</h3>
          <p class="small text-muted-2 mb-0">
            One column of headings, paragraphs and bullets, with no table, no text box and
            nothing a reader needs hidden in a page header. Those three are where an
            applicant-tracking system's parsing goes wrong.
          </p>
        </div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="col-md-4">
        <div class="glass-card h-100"><div class="card-body">
          <span class="icon-tile icon-tile-sm icon-navyblue mb-2"><i class="bi bi-sort-down"></i></span>
          <h3 class="h6 mb-1">Ordered against a role</h3>
          <p class="small text-muted-2 mb-0">
            Open it from an advert and the engagements that touched that advert's modules
            come first, marked as the relevant ones. Nothing is added or reworded.
          </p>
        </div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="glass-card mb-4"><div class="card-body">
      <h2 class="h5 mb-3">What it does not do</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>It writes nothing for you.</strong> Every line is something you typed or a
        label from the SAP catalogue. A generated summary is a claim you would be sending to
        an employer under your own name — and the first you would hear of a sentence you
        cannot stand behind is in the interview.
      </p>
      <p class="mb-0">
        There is no cover letter yet, for the same reason. Without your own words it would
        be a form letter, and a form letter is worse than no letter: it tells the reader
        you did not write to them.
      </p>
    </div></div>

    <div class="glass-card glass-card-tinted"><div class="card-body text-center py-4">
      <% if (currentUser && currentUser.isConsultant) { %>
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/profile/cv">Build your CV</a>
      <% } else if (currentUser) { %>
        <p class="text-muted-2 mb-0">
          The builder reads a consultant profile. Add the consultant role in
          <a href="/profile/settings">your settings</a> and it appears.
        </p>
      <% } else { %>
        <p class="text-muted-2 mb-3">Free, like everything else a consultant does here.</p>
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/auth/register">Create a free account</a>
        <a class="btn btn-outline-secondary" href="/jobs">Browse roles first</a>
      <% } %>
    </div></div>

  </div></div>
</div>
</section>
<%- include('../partials/layout-end') %>
